# --- Secrets ---
# Every .env variant (.env.local, .env.production, .env.bak …), not just the
# two spellings that used to be listed — a copied `.env.backup` holding the
# Apify token was one `git add -A` from being committed.
.env*
*.env
!.env.example
# Ad-hoc probe/experiment scripts at the repo root. These routinely get a real
# key pasted into them "just to test"; keeping them untracked means a stray
# `git add -A` can never publish one. Committed tooling lives in scripts/.
/test_*.py
/scratch*.py
/scratch*.mjs

# --- Personal data (real name/contact/EEO/salary answers) — keep local only ---
config/candidate.json
config/screening_answers.json
!config/candidate.example.json
!config/screening_answers.example.json

# Saved search profiles. These hold the same personal data candidate.json does
# -- name, contact details, work authorization, pay expectations -- and more of
# it, since a profile also stores the background parsed out of a resume. The
# taxonomy they are matched against (config/role_families.json) is shared,
# impersonal data and IS tracked.
config/profiles/
# Files regenerated from the active profile — derived, never edited by hand.
config/derived/

# Timestamped backups written by scripts/harvestSources.mjs --apply
config/*.bak

# --- Node ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- Local data & generated artifacts ---
.tmp/
coverage/
# EVERYTHING under data/ is local state — the SQLite store and its backups and
# sidecars, packets, run state, question queue, discovery caches, trackers.
# It used to be ignored file-by-file, and every new artifact (backup sidecars,
# source_timings.json, question_queue.json …) was committable until someone
# noticed and added a line. Now it is ignored unless deliberately re-included.
data/*
# Tracked inputs: the manual-jobs CSV and its example.
!data/jobs_input/
resumes/output/*
!resumes/output/.gitkeep
# Timestamped copies the tailoring step writes before touching the master.
# Generated artifacts, not sources.
resumes/base/history/
# THE MASTER RESUME IS PERSONAL DATA, NOT A SOURCE ARTIFACT.
# It was tracked for years because it is the only thing that makes the tailor
# testable — which put a real full name, personal mobile number, personal email,
# LinkedIn handle and a complete 10-year employment history into every clone of
# this repository. `MASTER_RESUME.example.docx` is a synthetic stand-in with the
# same structure; `npm run setup` copies it into place, and the tailor and its
# tests run against it unchanged.
# Carries YOUR facts into documents sent to employers: total years of
# experience, and the work-authorization sentence. It was tracked, so every
# clone shipped one person's "10+ years" and their H-1B wording.
config/cover_letter.json

resumes/base/MASTER_RESUME.docx
!resumes/base/MASTER_RESUME.example.docx
# A PDF rendered FROM the master. Derived, regenerated on demand, and a binary
# that would churn on every export.
resumes/base/MASTER_RESUME.pdf
applications/output/*
!applications/output/.gitkeep

# Each person's own workspace (src/profile/workspace.js): their master resume
# and history, tailored outputs and application packets. Personal, like the
# originals above. Their job databases live under data/ (already ignored).
resumes/profiles/
applications/profiles/
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
!logs/README.md

# --- Reports (generated output at the repo root ONLY — never src/reports/) ---
# Everything under reports/ is runtime output.
/reports/*

# --- Playwright ---
playwright-report/
test-results/
.cache/

# --- Browser profile (saved logins/cookies — never commit) ---
.browser-profile/
.browser-profile-*/

# --- Unrelated projects that happen to live under this checkout ---
# `git check-ignore PyProjects` matched nothing, so 34 MB of unrelated work
# (quant trading, stock analysis, a second job-search agent) sat untracked and
# un-ignored: one `git add -A` away from being committed here.
PyProjects/

# --- OS / Editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# Local Claude Code tooling: vendored skills/agents plus `.claude/worktrees/`,
# which holds real git worktrees. A worktree is a checkout, never a thing to
# commit into the repo it belongs to.
.claude/

# Design skills vendored by `npx skills add` (third-party Markdown, ~324 KB).
# Ignored like node_modules: the content is someone else's and reinstallable in
# one command. Its lockfile is local tooling state too.
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Local design sessions can include private screenshots and discussion.
.impeccable/

# Browser-automation session logs (Playwright MCP)
.playwright-mcp/

# One-file exports (npm run export) hold personal data.
exports/
*.jobagent
